141:The hyperparameters β rec and β kl control the balance between inference and sampling quality respectively. When β rec &gt; β kl , the optimization is focused on good reconstructions, which may lead to less variability in the generated samples, as latent posteriors are allowed to be very different from the prior. When β rec &lt; β kl , there will be more varied samples, but reconstruction quality will degrade.
145:As reported in the SIVAE paper Daniel and Tamar, 2021, the decoder tries to minimize the reconstruction error for generated data, which may slow down convergence, as at the beginning of the optimization the generated samples are of low quality. γ r is a hyperparameter that multiplies only the reconstruction term
